#category: alcohol
#source: USDA FoodData Central (SR Legacy)
#servings: 1 drink (150 ml)@150*;100 g@100
#density: 0.99
# ETHANOL IS 6.93 kcal/g AND IS NOT A MACRONUTRIENT FIELD.
# Every row here therefore fails a naive 4/4/9 energy check by design, and every
# row carries the `alcohol` exception. validate.mjs back-computes the implied
# ethanol content from the calorie gap and asserts it is physically plausible
# for the drink — that is a stronger check than 4/4/9 would have been.
# US standard drinks: beer 12 fl oz, wine 5 fl oz, spirits 1.5 fl oz.
# id|name|aliases|kcal|protein|carbs|fat|fiber|sugar|satfat|sodium|servings|extra

